<main id="main-content" tabindex="-1" class="v2-reference"><article><header class="article-top"><div class="article-intro"><a class="article-back" href="<?= e(url('/care-guide')) ?>">← <span>Back to the care notes</span></a><p class="eyebrow">THE ESSENTIALS</p><h1>A little care for your lengths.</h1><p>Conditioning has its own place in a wash-day routine. Keep the steps clear and the extras optional.</p><span class="article-meta">AVELA CARE NOTES · 2 MIN READ</span></div><div class="article-visual"><?= handoff_guide_art('condition') ?></div></header><div class="article-body"><nav class="article-outline" aria-label="In this note"><p class="eyebrow">IN THIS NOTE</p><a href="#note-0">Give conditioning its own step.</a><a href="#note-1">Be gentle with tangles.</a></nav><div class="article-copy"><section id="note-0"><h2>Give conditioning its own step.</h2><p>Conditioner follows washing. For curly or coily hair, the lengths may need more attention than just the tips. Check your product label for application and rinsing instructions.</p></section><section id="note-1"><h2>Be gentle with tangles.</h2><p>For curly hair, work through damp, conditioned sections gently with your fingers or a wide-tooth comb. Avoid pulling through knots or brushing dry curls forcefully.</p></section><div class="article-takeaway"><span class="eyebrow">A LITTLE TAKEAWAY</span><p>Leave-in care is an optional extra after washing and conditioning. Choose according to your hair and follow the product label.</p></div><div class="article-reference">Care reference<br><a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/hair-scalp-care/hair/curly-hair-care" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">American Academy of Dermatology · 6 curly hair care tips</a><p>General cosmetic care guidance. Avela does not diagnose or treat hair or scalp conditions.</p></div></div></div></article><section class="guide-cta"><div><h2>Make a little room for you.</h2><p>Bring what you know about your hair into your own routine.</p></div><a class="button primary" href="<?= e(url('/assessment')) ?>">Build my hair profile </a></section></main>
